# What NOT to ship inside the .vsix.
#
# `npm run bundle` produces a single out/extension.js, so the TypeScript sources, the
# unbundled per-file emit from `npm run compile`, and every development dependency are
# dead weight in the package. The negation on the next-to-last rule is what keeps the
# one file the manifest's `main` actually points at.

.vscode/**
.vscode-test/**
src/**
node_modules/**
**/*.ts
**/*.map
tsconfig.json
.gitignore
.eslintrc*
*.vsix

# Keep only the bundle from out/. Order matters: the exclusion is stated first and the
# single re-inclusion follows it.
out/**
!out/extension.js
